1
00:00:01,549 --> 00:00:02,675
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:03,468 --> 00:00:04,761
Earth...

3
00:00:05,512 --> 00:00:06,971
Fire...

4
00:00:07,805 --> 00:00:09,140
Air.

5
00:00:09,724 --> 00:00:13,019
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:14,145 --> 00:00:17,941
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:18,483 --> 00:00:21,945
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:25,698
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

9
00:00:25,823 --> 00:00:29,494
A hundred years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar...

10
00:00:29,619 --> 00:00:31,412
An airbender named Aang.

11
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,748
And although his airbending
skills are great,

12
00:00:33,873 --> 00:00:36,709
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

13
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:37,961
AANG: Oof!

14
00:00:38,044 --> 00:00:41,089
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

15
00:00:41,548 --> 00:00:43,299
( ♪... )

16
00:00:46,928 --> 00:00:49,013
( MAN READING )

17
00:00:49,847 --> 00:00:52,350
You have no idea what this war
has put me through.

18
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,893
Me personally.

19
00:00:54,310 --> 00:00:57,146
The Fire Nation took my mother
away from me.

20
00:00:58,189 --> 00:00:59,357
I'm sorry.

21
00:01:00,066 --> 00:01:03,570
You might have everyone else
here buying your transformation.

22
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:06,197
But you and I both know
you've struggled with doing

23
00:01:06,281 --> 00:01:07,740
the right thing in the past.

24
00:01:07,991 --> 00:01:10,285
So let me tell you something
right now.

25
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:14,455
You make one step backward, one slip-up,
give me one reason to think

26
00:01:14,539 --> 00:01:15,915
you might hurt Aang

27
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:19,377
And you won't have to worry
about your destiny anymore.

28
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:27,385
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

29
00:01:30,013 --> 00:01:33,016
( SNORING )

30
00:01:37,395 --> 00:01:38,771
( YAWNS )

31
00:01:40,648 --> 00:01:42,317
( APPA GRUNTS )

32
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:47,447
( APPA GROWLS )

33
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:10,053
ZUKO: Watch out!

34
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:11,721
( GRUNTING )

35
00:02:11,846 --> 00:02:13,222
What are you doing?

36
00:02:13,306 --> 00:02:14,724
Keeping rocks from crushing you.

37
00:02:15,183 --> 00:02:18,061
Okay, I'm not crushed,
you can get off me now.

38
00:02:18,603 --> 00:02:20,647
I'll take that as a thank you.

39
00:02:23,274 --> 00:02:25,109
Come on, we can get out
through here.

40
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,527
( MOMO CHATTERING )

41
00:02:26,819 --> 00:02:28,446
( GROANS ) What are you doing?

42
00:02:28,988 --> 00:02:31,115
Go ahead, I'll hold them off.

43
00:02:31,616 --> 00:02:33,409
I think this is a family visit.

44
00:02:33,534 --> 00:02:35,203
Zuko, no!

45
00:02:35,328 --> 00:02:37,497
Come on, we've got to
get out of here.

46
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,930
What are you doing here?

47
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,391
You mean it's not obvious yet?

48
00:02:56,516 --> 00:02:59,310
I am about to celebrate
becoming an only child.

49
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:06,401
( SHOUTS )

50
00:03:32,969 --> 00:03:34,303
( APPA GROANS )

51
00:03:34,512 --> 00:03:35,930
AANG: I can't get him
to go in there.

52
00:03:36,055 --> 00:03:37,557
Appa hates tunnels.

53
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:40,560
Aang, there's no way
we can fly out of here.

54
00:03:40,977 --> 00:03:42,645
AANG: We'll have to find a way.

55
00:03:43,104 --> 00:03:44,647
We need to split up.

56
00:03:44,772 --> 00:03:46,983
Take the tunnel and
get to the stolen airship.

57
00:03:48,317 --> 00:03:49,444
No.

58
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:52,363
The Fire Nation can't
separate our family again.

59
00:03:52,613 --> 00:03:53,990
It'll be okay.

60
00:03:54,073 --> 00:03:55,074
It's not forever.

61
00:04:11,257 --> 00:04:13,843
I can clear that away and
we can fly out through there.

62
00:04:13,926 --> 00:04:17,513
Um, there's an awful lot of fire
in that general direction.

63
00:04:17,889 --> 00:04:18,973
We'll get through.

64
00:04:19,098 --> 00:04:20,099
Let's go.

65
00:04:22,602 --> 00:04:24,061
( APPA GROWLING )

66
00:04:34,864 --> 00:04:36,741
( MOMO CHATTERING )

67
00:04:56,636 --> 00:04:57,845
( APPA GROANS )

68
00:04:58,304 --> 00:04:59,305
( GRUNTS )

69
00:04:59,388 --> 00:05:02,558
( APPA GROANING )

70
00:05:21,869 --> 00:05:23,412
( GRUNTING )

71
00:05:24,956 --> 00:05:27,625
( GRUNTING )

72
00:05:30,002 --> 00:05:31,921
( APPA GROANS )

73
00:05:36,008 --> 00:05:37,802
She's not gonna make it.

74
00:05:43,891 --> 00:05:45,643
Of course, she did.

75
00:05:47,311 --> 00:05:49,689
( APPA GROANS )

76
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:57,280
AANG: Wow, camping... It really seems like
old times again, doesn't it?

77
00:05:57,905 --> 00:06:01,117
If you really want it to feel
like old times, I could, uh...

78
00:06:01,242 --> 00:06:03,327
Chase you around awhile
and try to capture you.

79
00:06:03,452 --> 00:06:04,495
( LAUGHTER )

80
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:06,163
Ha-ha.

81
00:06:07,123 --> 00:06:09,625
( SIGHS ) To Zuko.

82
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:11,794
Who knew after all those times
he tried to snuff us out

83
00:06:11,919 --> 00:06:13,796
today he'd be our hero.

84
00:06:14,213 --> 00:06:15,673
ALL: Hear, hear.

85
00:06:16,799 --> 00:06:17,800
I'm touched.

86
00:06:18,092 --> 00:06:19,260
I don't deserve this.

87
00:06:19,677 --> 00:06:21,429
Yeah, no kidding.

88
00:06:23,139 --> 00:06:24,557
What's with her?

89
00:06:24,682 --> 00:06:26,142
I wish I knew.

90
00:06:28,269 --> 00:06:29,979
SOKKA: What's with him?

91
00:06:36,277 --> 00:06:37,778
This isn't fair.

92
00:06:38,029 --> 00:06:39,697
Everyone else
seems to trust me now.

93
00:06:39,864 --> 00:06:41,032
What is it with you?

94
00:06:41,115 --> 00:06:43,159
Oh, everyone trusts you now?

95
00:06:43,284 --> 00:06:45,578
I was the first person
to trust you, remember?

96
00:06:45,828 --> 00:06:47,288
Back in Ba Sing Se.

97
00:06:47,413 --> 00:06:50,499
And you turned around and
betrayed me, betrayed all of us.

98
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:53,336
What can I do
to make it up to you?

99
00:06:53,878 --> 00:06:55,129
You really want to know?

100
00:06:55,463 --> 00:06:59,216
Hmm, maybe you could reconquer Ba Sing Se
in the name of the Earth King.

101
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:02,053
Or, I know, you could
bring my mother back.

102
00:07:10,436 --> 00:07:11,562
Oops.

103
00:07:12,063 --> 00:07:13,230
Wrong tent.

104
00:07:13,481 --> 00:07:15,858
Sorry, do you need to
talk to Sokka too?

105
00:07:16,233 --> 00:07:17,860
Nope, not me.

106
00:07:21,906 --> 00:07:24,533
Well, hello.

107
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:28,704
Uh, Zuko, yes, why would I be
expecting anyone different?

108
00:07:28,829 --> 00:07:31,207
( GULPS, COUGHS )

109
00:07:31,374 --> 00:07:32,458
So what's on your mind?

110
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:36,253
Your sister, she hates me,
and I don't know why.

111
00:07:36,462 --> 00:07:38,172
But I do care
what she thinks of me.

112
00:07:38,547 --> 00:07:40,341
Nah, she doesn't hate you.

113
00:07:40,466 --> 00:07:42,093
Katara doesn't hate anyone.

114
00:07:42,426 --> 00:07:44,345
Except maybe some people
in the Fire Nation.

115
00:07:44,887 --> 00:07:48,057
No, I mean, uh, not people
who are good but used to be bad.

116
00:07:48,182 --> 00:07:49,892
I mean bad people.

117
00:07:50,142 --> 00:07:51,644
Fire Nation people who are still bad,

118
00:07:51,811 --> 00:07:53,604
who've never been good
and probably won't be ever.

119
00:07:53,688 --> 00:07:54,689
Stop.

120
00:07:55,106 --> 00:07:56,524
Okay, listen...

121
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:59,110
I know this may seem
out of nowhere

122
00:07:59,610 --> 00:08:01,696
but I want you to tell me
what happened to your mother.

123
00:08:01,988 --> 00:08:02,989
What?

124
00:08:03,197 --> 00:08:04,407
Why would you want to know that?

125
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:07,660
Katara mentioned it before when we were
in prison together in Ba Sing Se

126
00:08:08,202 --> 00:08:10,329
and again just now
when she was yelling at me.

127
00:08:10,955 --> 00:08:12,748
I think somehow...

128
00:08:13,082 --> 00:08:16,252
She's connected her anger
about that to her anger at me.

129
00:08:17,628 --> 00:08:19,380
It's not a day I like to remember.

130
00:08:26,345 --> 00:08:28,305
( LAUGHING )

131
00:08:34,186 --> 00:08:36,230
I'm going to find mom.

132
00:08:39,025 --> 00:08:41,485
SOKKA: Many of the warriors had
seen the black snow before

133
00:08:41,610 --> 00:08:43,529
and they knew what it meant...

134
00:08:43,654 --> 00:08:45,448
A Fire Nation raid.

135
00:08:45,573 --> 00:08:47,366
( SCREAMING )

136
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,913
( SCREAMING )

137
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:59,962
SOKKA: We were badly outnumbered,
but somehow we managed to drive them off.

138
00:09:04,341 --> 00:09:07,094
As quickly as they came,
they just left.

139
00:09:10,598 --> 00:09:12,933
I was so relieved
when it was over

140
00:09:13,059 --> 00:09:15,311
but that's because I didn't
know yet what had happened.

141
00:09:16,228 --> 00:09:18,105
I didn't know
we'd lost our mother.

142
00:09:18,481 --> 00:09:22,443
Wait, can you remember any details about
the soldiers who raided your village?

143
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,029
Like what the lead ship
looked like?

144
00:09:25,488 --> 00:09:27,907
Yeah... Sea ravens.

145
00:09:28,074 --> 00:09:30,493
The main ship had flags
with sea ravens on them.

146
00:09:31,035 --> 00:09:32,828
The symbol of
the southern raiders.

147
00:09:33,662 --> 00:09:34,747
Thanks, Sokka.

148
00:09:34,872 --> 00:09:36,123
No problem.

149
00:09:36,248 --> 00:09:38,459
Thanks for stopping by.

150
00:09:38,876 --> 00:09:40,753
( SIGHS ) Thought
he'd never leave.

151
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,215
Suki?

152
00:09:45,883 --> 00:09:47,718
( WHISTLING )

153
00:09:56,352 --> 00:09:57,728
You look terrible.

154
00:09:58,354 --> 00:09:59,730
I waited out here all night.

155
00:09:59,939 --> 00:10:01,190
What do you want?

156
00:10:01,524 --> 00:10:03,234
I know who killed your mother.

157
00:10:03,317 --> 00:10:04,693
I'm going to help you find him.

158
00:10:14,829 --> 00:10:16,372
I need to borrow Appa.

159
00:10:16,956 --> 00:10:19,834
Why, is it your turn to take
a little field trip with Zuko?

160
00:10:20,084 --> 00:10:21,752
Yes, it is.

161
00:10:22,837 --> 00:10:25,256
Oh... What's going on?

162
00:10:25,464 --> 00:10:28,008
We're going to find the man
who took my mother from me.

163
00:10:28,676 --> 00:10:30,427
ZUKO: Sokka told me
the story of what happened.

164
00:10:30,636 --> 00:10:33,430
I know who did it,
and I know how to find him.

165
00:10:33,681 --> 00:10:36,851
Um, and what exactly do you
think this will accomplish?

166
00:10:37,810 --> 00:10:40,187
( SCOFFS ) I knew
you wouldn't understand.

167
00:10:40,729 --> 00:10:43,274
Wait, stop, I do understand.

168
00:10:43,607 --> 00:10:45,776
You're feeling unbelievable
pain and rage.

169
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:49,446
How do you think I felt about
the sandbenders when they stole Appa?

170
00:10:50,156 --> 00:10:51,949
How do you think I felt
about the Fire Nation

171
00:10:52,032 --> 00:10:53,826
when I found out what happened
to my people?

172
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,536
ZUKO: She needs this, Aang.

173
00:10:55,661 --> 00:10:58,247
This is about getting closure
and justice.

174
00:10:58,372 --> 00:10:59,623
I don't think so.

175
00:10:59,748 --> 00:11:01,500
I think it's about
getting revenge.

176
00:11:01,625 --> 00:11:02,835
KATARA: Fine, maybe it is.

177
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,753
Maybe that's what I need.

178
00:11:04,879 --> 00:11:06,755
Maybe that's what he deserves.

179
00:11:06,881 --> 00:11:09,133
Katara, you sound like Jet.

180
00:11:09,258 --> 00:11:10,467
It's not the same.

181
00:11:10,676 --> 00:11:11,969
Jet attacked the innocent.

182
00:11:12,178 --> 00:11:14,180
This man, he's a monster.

183
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:16,223
Katara, she was my mother too.

184
00:11:16,473 --> 00:11:18,559
But I think Aang might be right.

185
00:11:19,059 --> 00:11:20,895
Then you didn't love her
the way I did.

186
00:11:21,187 --> 00:11:22,479
Katara...

187
00:11:23,814 --> 00:11:27,318
The monks used to say that revenge
is like a two-headed rat viper.

188
00:11:27,902 --> 00:11:30,905
While you watch your enemy go down,
you're being poisoned yourself.

189
00:11:31,572 --> 00:11:34,283
That's cute, but this isn't
air temple preschool.

190
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,118
It's the real world.

191
00:11:36,243 --> 00:11:38,162
Now that I know
he's out there...

192
00:11:38,287 --> 00:11:40,122
Now that I know
we can find him...

193
00:11:40,247 --> 00:11:41,874
I feel like I have no choice.

194
00:11:42,416 --> 00:11:44,668
Katara, you do have a choice.

195
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,212
Forgiveness.

196
00:11:46,462 --> 00:11:48,214
That's the same as
doing nothing.

197
00:11:48,547 --> 00:11:50,132
No, it's not.

198
00:11:50,424 --> 00:11:53,802
It's easy to do nothing,
but it's hard to forgive.

199
00:11:53,928 --> 00:11:57,181
It's not just hard,
it's impossible.

200
00:12:07,775 --> 00:12:09,985
So you were just gonna
take Appa anyway?

201
00:12:10,945 --> 00:12:11,946
Yes.

202
00:12:12,154 --> 00:12:14,448
It's okay, because I forgive you.

203
00:12:15,866 --> 00:12:17,451
That give you any ideas?

204
00:12:17,618 --> 00:12:19,119
Don't try to stop us.

205
00:12:19,495 --> 00:12:21,205
I wasn't planning to.

206
00:12:21,330 --> 00:12:23,123
This is a journey
you need to take.

207
00:12:23,249 --> 00:12:25,042
You need to face this man.

208
00:12:27,253 --> 00:12:30,297
But when you do,
please don't choose revenge.

209
00:12:30,547 --> 00:12:33,467
Let your anger out,
and then let it go.

210
00:12:34,009 --> 00:12:35,135
Forgive him.

211
00:12:35,302 --> 00:12:38,514
Okay, we'll be sure to do that,
guru goody-goody.

212
00:12:38,764 --> 00:12:40,266
Thanks for understanding, Aang.

213
00:12:40,474 --> 00:12:41,517
Yip-yip.

214
00:12:42,184 --> 00:12:43,519
( APPA GROANING )

215
00:12:43,894 --> 00:12:45,646
You know, you're pretty wise
for a kid.

216
00:12:46,355 --> 00:12:47,481
Thanks, Sokka.

217
00:12:47,564 --> 00:12:49,858
Usually it's annoying, but
right now I'm just impressed.

218
00:12:50,192 --> 00:12:51,568
I appreciate that.

219
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:53,779
So can I borrow Momo for a week?

220
00:12:54,071 --> 00:12:55,155
Why do you need Momo?

221
00:12:55,281 --> 00:12:56,448
( HUMS ) I don't know.

222
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:02,371
ZUKO: We need to find the
fire navy communication tower.

223
00:13:02,663 --> 00:13:05,582
All the navy's movements are
coordinated by messenger hawk.

224
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:08,669
And every tower has to be up to date
on where everyone is deployed.

225
00:13:09,295 --> 00:13:11,171
KATARA: So once we find
the communication tower

226
00:13:11,255 --> 00:13:13,382
we bust in and take
the information we need.

227
00:13:13,841 --> 00:13:15,134
ZUKO: Not exactly.

228
00:13:15,217 --> 00:13:17,720
We need to be stealthy
and make sure no one spots us.

229
00:13:18,137 --> 00:13:21,890
Otherwise, they'll warn the southern
raiders long before we reach them.

230
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,402
( DOOR CREAKS )

231
00:13:47,708 --> 00:13:50,169
Okay, southern raiders.

232
00:13:52,338 --> 00:13:55,341
Bam, on patrol
near Whaletail Island.

233
00:13:56,175 --> 00:13:57,968
Whaletail Island,
here we come.

234
00:13:59,511 --> 00:14:01,847
( APPA GROANS )

235
00:14:06,977 --> 00:14:08,187
You should get some rest.

236
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:09,813
We'll be there in a few hours.

237
00:14:10,314 --> 00:14:11,607
You'll need all your strength.

238
00:14:12,066 --> 00:14:13,776
Oh, don't you worry
about my strength.

239
00:14:13,901 --> 00:14:15,027
I have plenty.

240
00:14:15,361 --> 00:14:17,905
I'm not the helpless little girl
I was when they came.

241
00:14:22,034 --> 00:14:24,745
I'm going to find mom.

242
00:14:27,706 --> 00:14:29,500
Mom!

243
00:14:31,585 --> 00:14:33,128
MOTHER: Just let her go...

244
00:14:33,212 --> 00:14:35,089
and I'll give you
the information you want.

245
00:14:35,422 --> 00:14:37,758
You heard your mother...
Get out of here!

246
00:14:38,133 --> 00:14:40,010
Mom, I'm scared.

247
00:14:40,219 --> 00:14:41,387
Go find your dad, sweetie.

248
00:14:41,512 --> 00:14:42,513
I'll handle this.

249
00:14:50,437 --> 00:14:52,314
KATARA: I ran
as fast as I could.

250
00:14:52,481 --> 00:14:54,108
Dad, dad!

251
00:14:54,191 --> 00:14:55,984
Please, I think mom's
in trouble!

252
00:14:56,276 --> 00:14:57,444
There's a man in our house.

253
00:14:57,778 --> 00:14:58,821
Kya!

254
00:15:02,741 --> 00:15:04,410
KATARA: But we were too late.

255
00:15:05,119 --> 00:15:07,079
When we got there,
the man was gone...

256
00:15:07,663 --> 00:15:09,039
And so was she.

257
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,166
Your mother was a brave woman.

258
00:15:13,794 --> 00:15:14,878
I know.

259
00:15:20,384 --> 00:15:22,636
There, see those
sea raven flags?

260
00:15:26,515 --> 00:15:28,142
ZUKO: It's the southern raiders.

261
00:15:28,350 --> 00:15:29,893
Let's do this.

262
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:39,862
So there I was, and I was like,
you know, it was...

263
00:15:39,987 --> 00:15:41,447
( SCREAMS )

264
00:15:53,125 --> 00:15:54,376
( SCREAMING )

265
00:15:57,379 --> 00:15:59,214
( APPA SNORTS )

266
00:16:01,175 --> 00:16:02,759
( SCREAMS )

267
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:07,431
( MAN GRUNTS )

268
00:16:12,311 --> 00:16:13,979
This is it, Katara.

269
00:16:14,062 --> 00:16:15,564
Are you ready to face him?

270
00:16:18,442 --> 00:16:19,443
( ROARS )

271
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:33,248
Who are you?

272
00:16:33,332 --> 00:16:34,541
You don't remember her?

273
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:36,376
You will soon, trust me.

274
00:16:40,088 --> 00:16:41,298
What's...

275
00:16:41,381 --> 00:16:43,342
( GRUNTING )

276
00:16:44,218 --> 00:16:45,552
Happening to me?

277
00:16:47,179 --> 00:16:48,347
( GROANS )

278
00:16:51,975 --> 00:16:53,101
Think back.

279
00:16:53,268 --> 00:16:56,063
Think back to your last raid
on the southern water tribe.

280
00:16:56,772 --> 00:16:58,607
I don't know what
you're talking about.

281
00:16:58,690 --> 00:17:00,067
Please, I don't know.

282
00:17:00,776 --> 00:17:02,027
Don't lie!

283
00:17:02,236 --> 00:17:05,072
You look her in the eye and you tell me
you don't remember what you did.

284
00:17:15,123 --> 00:17:16,208
It's not him.

285
00:17:17,876 --> 00:17:19,086
( GRUNTS )

286
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:20,879
He's not the man.

287
00:17:21,004 --> 00:17:22,005
What?

288
00:17:22,089 --> 00:17:23,215
What do you mean he's not?

289
00:17:23,382 --> 00:17:24,883
He's the leader of
the southern raiders.

290
00:17:24,967 --> 00:17:26,301
He has to be the guy.

291
00:17:31,014 --> 00:17:32,266
( GRUNTING )

292
00:17:32,349 --> 00:17:34,643
If you're not the man
we're looking for, who is?

293
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:37,062
You must be looking for Yon Rha.

294
00:17:37,396 --> 00:17:39,231
He retired four years ago.

295
00:17:51,368 --> 00:17:55,205
Yon Rha, you lazy piece of work,
I need something.

296
00:17:55,664 --> 00:17:56,999
Yes, mother.

297
00:17:57,499 --> 00:17:58,709
What is it?

298
00:17:58,875 --> 00:18:02,170
The tomato-carrot from your
garden are too hard for my gums.

299
00:18:02,379 --> 00:18:04,214
I need something soft and juicy.

300
00:18:04,923 --> 00:18:07,551
Would you like something else
from the garden?

301
00:18:07,759 --> 00:18:09,052
I would be happy to...

302
00:18:09,177 --> 00:18:10,512
Forget your stupid garden!

303
00:18:11,013 --> 00:18:14,391
Get your grimy heinie to the market
and buy me some real food.

304
00:18:17,811 --> 00:18:21,398
( THUNDER RUMBLING FAINTLY )

305
00:18:21,648 --> 00:18:24,526
( WIND CHIMES RINGING )

306
00:18:30,907 --> 00:18:32,159
Hello?

307
00:18:32,534 --> 00:18:34,119
Did you see someone?

308
00:18:44,463 --> 00:18:45,464
Hello?

309
00:18:45,672 --> 00:18:46,840
Is someone there?

310
00:18:50,052 --> 00:18:51,303
That was him.

311
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:53,305
That was the monster.

312
00:18:58,602 --> 00:19:01,480
( THUNDER RUMBLING )

313
00:19:05,901 --> 00:19:07,986
Nobody sneaks up on me
without getting burned.

314
00:19:19,414 --> 00:19:20,791
( GRUNTS )

315
00:19:25,796 --> 00:19:27,673
We weren't behind the bush.

316
00:19:28,715 --> 00:19:31,009
And I wouldn't try
firebending again.

317
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:34,888
Whoever you are, take my money,
take whatever you want.

318
00:19:35,097 --> 00:19:36,598
I'll cooperate.

319
00:19:38,016 --> 00:19:39,685
Do you know who I am?

320
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:42,521
No... I'm not sure.

321
00:19:42,896 --> 00:19:45,607
Oh, you better remember me
like your life depends on it.

322
00:19:45,899 --> 00:19:47,776
Why don't you take
a closer look?

323
00:19:48,318 --> 00:19:52,280
Yes, yes, I remember you now.

324
00:19:53,073 --> 00:19:54,991
You're the little
water tribe girl.

325
00:19:55,367 --> 00:19:57,035
( THUNDER CRASHES )

326
00:19:57,119 --> 00:19:59,621
Just let her go and I'll give
you the information you want.

327
00:19:59,955 --> 00:20:01,164
You heard your mother.

328
00:20:01,456 --> 00:20:03,041
Get out of here.

329
00:20:03,125 --> 00:20:05,001
Mom, I'm scared.

330
00:20:05,168 --> 00:20:06,586
Go find your dad, sweetie.

331
00:20:06,753 --> 00:20:08,088
I'll handle this.

332
00:20:11,466 --> 00:20:14,594
Now tell me...
Who is it?

333
00:20:15,011 --> 00:20:16,888
Who's the waterbender?

334
00:20:17,139 --> 00:20:19,683
There are no waterbenders here.

335
00:20:19,891 --> 00:20:22,769
The Fire Nation took them
all away a long time ago.

336
00:20:22,894 --> 00:20:23,937
You're lying.

337
00:20:24,187 --> 00:20:29,151
My source says there's one waterbender
left in the southern water tribe.

338
00:20:29,276 --> 00:20:32,612
We're not leaving
until we find the waterbender.

339
00:20:32,821 --> 00:20:36,241
If I tell you, do you promise to leave
the rest of the village alone?

340
00:20:37,242 --> 00:20:38,702
Mm.

341
00:20:39,828 --> 00:20:42,289
It's me... Take me
as your prisoner.

342
00:20:42,706 --> 00:20:45,751
I'm afraid I'm not
taking prisoners today.

343
00:20:48,336 --> 00:20:49,337
( GULPS )

344
00:20:50,005 --> 00:20:51,006
( THUNDER CRASHES )

345
00:20:51,089 --> 00:20:52,132
She lied to you.

346
00:20:52,215 --> 00:20:54,217
She was protecting
the last waterbender.

347
00:20:54,301 --> 00:20:55,302
What?

348
00:20:55,469 --> 00:20:56,511
Who?

349
00:20:57,721 --> 00:20:58,722
Me!

350
00:21:12,194 --> 00:21:13,361
( GRUNTS )

351
00:21:14,196 --> 00:21:15,322
( WHIMPERS )

352
00:21:28,835 --> 00:21:32,672
I did a bad thing, I know I did,
and you deserve revenge.

353
00:21:32,798 --> 00:21:34,508
So why don't you take my mother?

354
00:21:34,591 --> 00:21:35,759
That would be fair.

355
00:21:36,343 --> 00:21:39,304
I always wondered what kind of
person could do such a thing.

356
00:21:39,763 --> 00:21:42,641
But now that I see you,
I think I understand.

357
00:21:43,141 --> 00:21:46,770
There's just nothing inside you,
nothing at all.

358
00:21:47,062 --> 00:21:49,272
You're pathetic and sad
and empty.

359
00:21:49,356 --> 00:21:51,983
Please spare me. ( WHIMPERS )

360
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:54,486
But as much as I hate you...

361
00:21:56,196 --> 00:21:57,864
I just can't do it.

362
00:22:04,454 --> 00:22:07,040
( YON RHA WHIMPERING )

363
00:22:17,467 --> 00:22:18,677
( APPA GROANS )

364
00:22:25,350 --> 00:22:27,143
Katara, are you okay?

365
00:22:28,228 --> 00:22:29,563
I'm doing fine.

366
00:22:30,939 --> 00:22:32,607
Zuko told me what you did.

367
00:22:32,983 --> 00:22:34,776
Or what you didn't do, I guess.

368
00:22:35,318 --> 00:22:36,403
I'm proud of you.

369
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:38,530
I wanted to do it.

370
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:42,033
I wanted to take out all my
anger at him, but I couldn't.

371
00:22:42,868 --> 00:22:45,579
I don't know if it's
because I'm too weak to do it

372
00:22:45,662 --> 00:22:48,039
or if it's because
I'm strong enough not to.

373
00:22:48,373 --> 00:22:49,666
AANG: You did the right thing.

374
00:22:49,875 --> 00:22:53,044
Forgiveness is the first step you have
to take to begin healing.

375
00:22:55,380 --> 00:22:58,758
But I didn't forgive him...
I'll never forgive him.

376
00:23:01,011 --> 00:23:03,179
But I am ready to forgive you.

377
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:12,063
ZUKO: You were right
about what Katara needed.

378
00:23:12,689 --> 00:23:14,274
Violence wasn't the answer.

379
00:23:14,816 --> 00:23:16,151
It never is.

380
00:23:16,651 --> 00:23:18,653
Then I have a question for you.

381
00:23:19,738 --> 00:23:21,656
What are you gonna do
when you face my father?

382
00:23:33,251 --> 00:23:36,004
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
